Build a simple authentication layer for the existing React + Vite frontend.

Requirements:

GOAL:

* protect the demo application with a login page
* login required only in deployed environments
* local development should automatically bypass login

AUTH FLOW:

* user enters username + password
* frontend validates credentials against Vercel environment variables
* if valid:

  * store authenticated session in localStorage
  * redirect to main app
* if invalid:

  * show error message

LOCAL DEVELOPMENT:
If running locally:

* automatically bypass login
* no login screen shown

Detect local environment using:

* localhost
* import.meta.env.DEV

ENV VARIABLES:
Use Vercel environment variables:

* VITE_DEMO_USERNAME
* VITE_DEMO_PASSWORD

IMPORTANT:

* keep implementation SIMPLE
* this is demo protection only
* no JWT
* no backend auth
* no database
* no OAuth

ROUTES:

* /login
* /
* unauthenticated users redirected to /login

UI REQUIREMENTS:

* centered login card
* modern clean design
* Tailwind only
* responsive
* logo/title section
* username input
* password input
* login button
* loading state
* invalid credentials message

CREATE:

* LoginPage component
* AuthContext or lightweight auth hook
* ProtectedRoute component
* auth utility functions

SESSION:

* persist login across refresh
* logout button in app header

LOGOUT:

* clear localStorage
* redirect to /login

SECURITY:

* do not expose passwords in UI
* use environment variables only
* do not hardcode credentials

IMPORTANT:

* preserve existing OCR app functionality
* integrate cleanly into current architecture
* minimal code changes to existing pages
